      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\n# pthread_setspecific (enabled with CONFIG_POSIX_THREADS) allocates memory from\n# kernel memory pool to store thread local data of\n# sizeof(struct pthread_key_data) bytes for every unique \u003ckey, thread\u003e:\n# https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/9c2983926a4c95d6896d0c9aa63dfcc9c42a6d97/lib/posix/options/key.c#L210-L211\n# The only use of pthread_setspecific that we have is in BoringSSL, which uses a\n# single pthread_key_t:\n# https://crsrc.org/o/src/third_party/boringssl/crypto/thread_pthread.c;l\u003d98-107;drc\u003d04c3d40f0695b07b9795e8a69a3babeab52b861f.\n# However, HEAP_MEM_POOL_ADD_SIZE_POSIX_THREADS, defaults to 256, which forces\n# that as a minimum value due to this logic:\n# https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/e1f258d8e21f30d9272b65bf59a0030519adf82e/kernel/Kconfig#L757-L763\n```",
